WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.643 --> 00:00:15.985
In the summer Diana Barry had a party.

2
00:00:16.005 --> 00:00:22.892
"There will just be the girls in our class," Anne assured Marilla since Marilla knew that Anne had

3
00:00:22.932 --> 00:00:24.573
a habit of getting into trouble.

4
00:00:25.294 --> 00:00:27.296
The girls played in the Barrys' garden.

5
00:00:27.992 --> 00:00:32.335
After a while they grew tired of all their games and were ready for mischief.

6
00:00:33.096 --> 00:00:39.059
They soon decided to play "dares," which involved daring one's friends to try something risky.

7
00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:46.464
First Carrie Sloane dared Ruby Gillis to climb the huge willow tree that was infested with fat, green

8
00:00:46.544 --> 00:00:51.788
caterpillars. Much to everyone's surprise, Ruby bravely climbed the tree.

9
00:00:52.528 --> 00:00:58.393
Then Josie Pye dared Jane Andrews to hop around the garden on her left foot without stopping.

10
00:00:59.153 --> 00:01:02.416
Jane Andrews tried but gave up at the third corner.

11
00:01:03.137 --> 00:01:07.000
Josie Pye gloated because Jane Andrews could not do her dare.

12
00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:14.105
Anne saw Josie Pye gloating and quickly dared Josie to walk along the top of the Barrys' garden

13
00:01:14.185 --> 00:01:22.002
fence. Walking along fences requires some skill, but unfortunately Josie Pye had a natural ability for walking on

14
00:01:22.062 --> 00:01:26.504
fences. The girls reluctantly admired Josie's skill and bravery.

15
00:01:27.244 --> 00:01:31.486
Josie came down, flushed with victory, and gave Anne a defiant look.

16
00:01:32.846 --> 00:01:34.367
Anne tossed her red braids.

17
00:01:34.387 --> 00:01:40.610
"I don't think it's anything fantastic to walk on such a little, low fence," she said.

18
00:01:40.630 --> 00:01:44.391
"I knew a girl who could walk on a rooftop."

19
00:01:44.411 --> 00:01:47.688
"I don't believe it," said Josie flatly.

20
00:01:47.708 --> 00:01:51.510
"You couldn't walk on a rooftop anyhow," she added.

21
00:01:51.530 --> 00:01:53.050
"Couldn't I?"

22
00:01:53.490 --> 00:01:55.030
said Anne, without thinking.

23
00:01:55.051 --> 00:01:58.852
"Then I dare you," said Josie, sneering.

24
00:01:58.872 --> 00:02:04.713
"I dare you to climb up there and walk along the top of the Barrys' kitchen roof."

25
00:02:05.553 --> 00:02:08.514
Anne turned pale, but she walked towards the house.

26
00:02:09.215 --> 00:02:11.175
There was a ladder leaning against the wall.

27
00:02:11.195 --> 00:02:14.116
"Don't do it, Anne," pleaded Diana.

28
00:02:14.796 --> 00:02:16.517
"You'll fall off and be killed.

29
00:02:17.157 --> 00:02:18.537
Never mind Josie Pye.

30
00:02:18.557 --> 00:02:22.478
It isn't fair to dare anybody to do anything so dangerous."

31
00:02:22.498 --> 00:02:24.779
"I must do it.

32
00:02:25.439 --> 00:02:28.780
My honor is at stake," said Anne solemnly.

33
00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:33.222
"If I am killed, you can have my pearl bead ring."

34
00:02:33.942 --> 00:02:38.863
Anne climbed the ladder, balanced herself on the rooftop, and started to walk along it.

35
00:02:39.543 --> 00:02:40.844
She was very high.

36
00:02:41.596 --> 00:02:46.440
Anne realized that imagination did not help much when you were walking on a roof.

37
00:02:47.161 --> 00:02:52.024
Nevertheless she managed to take several steps before the catastrophe came.

38
00:02:52.725 --> 00:02:58.450
She swayed and then fell, sliding off the roof and landing headfirst in a garden of vines.

39
00:02:59.370 --> 00:03:01.092
The girls below screamed.

40
00:03:01.732 --> 00:03:08.838
When Diana and the other girls—except for Ruby Gillis, who had gone into hysterics—rushed around the house, they

41
00:03:08.898 --> 00:03:11.200
found Anne lying in the tangled vines.

42
00:03:11.984 --> 00:03:13.725
She was very pale and limp.

43
00:03:13.745 --> 00:03:15.845
"Anne, are you dead?"

44
00:03:16.385 --> 00:03:19.806
shrieked Diana, throwing herself on her knees beside Anne.

45
00:03:21.066 --> 00:03:22.467
Anne sat up, dizzy.

46
00:03:22.487 --> 00:03:26.388
"No, Diana," she said uncertainly.

47
00:03:26.408 --> 00:03:31.749
"I am not dead, but I think I am unconscious."

48
00:03:32.710 --> 00:03:37.511
The girls were immensely relieved by Anne's words, especially Josie Pye.

49
00:03:38.151 --> 00:03:38.671
When Mrs.

50
00:03:38.731 --> 00:03:44.246
Barry appeared, Anne tried to get to her feet, but she fell back with a sharp little cry

51
00:03:44.306 --> 00:03:44.767
of pain.

52
00:03:44.787 --> 00:03:46.629
"What's the matter?

53
00:03:47.610 --> 00:03:48.811
Where have you hurt yourself?"

54
00:03:49.251 --> 00:03:50.172
demanded Mrs.

55
00:03:50.232 --> 00:03:54.056
Barry. "My ankle," gasped Anne.

56
00:03:54.756 --> 00:03:57.639
Marilla was in the orchard when she saw Mr.

57
00:03:57.699 --> 00:03:58.120
and Mrs.

58
00:03:58.180 --> 00:04:01.263
Barry and a procession of girls coming toward the house.

59
00:04:02.123 --> 00:04:06.648
Mr. Barry carried Anne in his arms, with her head limp against his shoulder.

60
00:04:07.408 --> 00:04:10.169
At that moment Marilla had a revelation.

61
00:04:11.130 --> 00:04:16.972
Before, she had admitted that she liked Anne—no, that she was very fond of Anne.

62
00:04:17.672 --> 00:04:21.714
But now she knew that Anne was dearer to her than anything on earth.

63
00:04:21.734 --> 00:04:24.415
"Mrs. Barry, what happened?"

64
00:04:25.596 --> 00:04:26.456
Marilla gasped.

65
00:04:27.116 --> 00:04:30.718
Mrs. Barry had never seen Marilla look so pale and anxious.

66
00:04:31.518 --> 00:04:33.919
Anne herself answered, lifting her head.

67
00:04:33.939 --> 00:04:36.120
"Don't be frightened, Marilla.

68
00:04:36.836 --> 00:04:40.458
I was walking on the Barrys' roof, and I fell off.

69
00:04:41.699 --> 00:04:44.040
I think I sprained my ankle.

70
00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:48.542
However, I could have broken my neck, but I didn't.

71
00:04:49.323 --> 00:04:50.844
Let's look on the bright side!"

72
00:04:51.584 --> 00:04:53.985
Marilla felt the blood return to her face.

73
00:04:54.726 --> 00:04:56.867
Mr. Barry carried Anne into the house.

74
00:04:57.627 --> 00:05:01.209
Later the doctor came and announced that Anne had broken her ankle.

75
00:05:01.229 --> 00:05:05.111
"Don't you feel sorry for me, Marilla?"

76
00:05:05.532 --> 00:05:06.152
Anne asked.

77
00:05:06.908 --> 00:05:09.589
"It was your own fault," answered Marilla.

78
00:05:09.609 --> 00:05:12.951
"That's exactly why you should feel sorry for me.

79
00:05:12.971 --> 00:05:18.533
If I could blame somebody, I would feel so much better," Anne said.

80
00:05:18.553 --> 00:05:23.675
"What would you do, Marilla, if someone dared you to walk on the roof?"

81
00:05:23.695 --> 00:05:28.717
"I would stay on the ground and let them dare," Marilla shot back.

82
00:05:28.737 --> 00:05:35.880
"You're strong, Marilla, but I couldn't bear Josie Pye's scorn," Anne said.

83
00:05:36.648 --> 00:05:40.412
"And I think I've been punished enough, so you don't have to punish me.

84
00:05:41.072 --> 00:05:44.735
It hurt dreadfully when the doctor set my ankle in plaster.

85
00:05:45.516 --> 00:05:49.880
I'll miss six weeks of school, and I'll miss the new lady teacher.

86
00:05:50.621 --> 00:05:53.083
She won't be new by the time I'm at school.

87
00:05:53.744 --> 00:05:58.908
And Gilbert—I mean, everybody—will get ahead of me in class."

88
00:05:59.809 --> 00:06:02.752
Over the next six weeks, Anne had many visitors.

89
00:06:03.504 --> 00:06:08.585
Not a day passed without one or more of the schoolgirls dropping in to bring her flowers and

90
00:06:08.665 --> 00:06:11.146
books and tell her the news of Avonlea.

91
00:06:11.746 --> 00:06:16.768
Diana, Anne's most faithful friend, visited every day after school.

92
00:06:17.568 --> 00:06:19.268
Even Josie Pye visited once.

93
00:06:19.989 --> 00:06:23.850
Anne happily realized that she had many kind friends and neighbors.

94
00:06:24.910 --> 00:06:30.271
One day, after the visitors had left, Anne chatted to Marilla about the news from school.

95
00:06:30.892 --> 00:06:35.430
The new teacher had arrived, and all the girls thought she was perfectly sweet.

96
00:06:36.110 --> 00:06:41.394
She dressed beautifully, and her sleeve puffs were bigger than anybody else's in Avonlea.

97
00:06:41.414 --> 00:06:48.179
"On Friday mornings, Marilla," Anne said, "everybody has to recite a poem or a story.

98
00:06:48.199 --> 00:06:50.020
How exciting!

99
00:06:51.461 --> 00:06:59.146
On Friday afternoons Miss Stacy, the new teacher, takes everyone to the woods for a 'field day,' and

100
00:06:59.166 --> 00:07:01.908
they study ferns and flowers and birds.

101
00:07:02.656 --> 00:07:07.318
And they have physical education exercises every morning and afternoon.

102
00:07:07.338 --> 00:07:12.360
Mrs. Lynde says it's ridiculous, but I think it's splendid.

103
00:07:13.060 --> 00:07:16.301
I believe Miss Stacy will be a kindred spirit."

104
00:07:16.321 --> 00:07:20.222
"There's one thing that's quite clear, Anne," said Marilla.

105
00:07:20.242 --> 00:07:24.084
"Falling off the Barrys' roof hasn't injured your tongue."
